OL,3,GNEWSAIllegal e-bikes 'menace' impacts
OL,4,Alegitimate sales
OL,5,
OL,6,FA cycle shop business says staff often
OL,7,Fface aggression from customers when
OL,8,Fthey refuse to repair illegal e-bikes
OL,9,Fon health and safety grounds.
OL,11,FRichardsons Cycles, an independent
OL,12,Fsales and repair shop with branches in
OL,13,FPeterborough, Cambridgeshire,
OL,14,FNorthamptonshire and Norfolk, said the
OL,15,Frise in illegal e-bikes was also
OL,16,Faffecting sales of legal electric
OL,17,Fcycles.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,375,370,200,160,0,100
PN,37402
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F374A1787721999
OL,1,W5j 5Qws js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-, *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSAIllegal e-bikes 'menace' impacts
OL,4,Alegitimate sales
OL,5,
OL,6,FCarmen Orga, of Pearl and Parker, which
OL,7,Fowns the business, said repair requests
OL,8,Fhad become "a real issue", adding that
OL,9,Fsome customers "get aggressive" on
OL,10,Frefusal.
OL,12,FPeterborough's Labour MP, Andrew Pakes,
OL,13,Fis calling on the government to ban the
OL,14,Fsale of illegal e-bikes and the
OL,15,Fconversion kits used to build them,
OL,16,Fdescribing them as a "menace".
